{"id":"u-6af9773a-637f-497f-8141-27ece1209576","src":"community","title":"PPL Hypertrophy","author":"Joshua B.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/HST1Sa-ppl-hypertrophy","desc":"This program is split up into three hypertrophy blocks that have two variations of PPL repeated during the accumulation week.\n\nBetween each PPL rest 1-2 days as needed, generally later in the block as RPE goes higher you'll likely need 2 days of rest between each PPL.\n\nThis phase prioritizes quads/squats and triceps, prioritizing different muscle groups can help bring up weaknesses and/or to prevent psychological and physiological staleness. \n\nHypertrophy blocks help with: building muscle, preventing staleness, and preventing over use injuries.\n\nIncluding non-competitive movements with higher rep ranges with a controlled eccentrics that prioritizes technique and full ROM to enhance hypertrophy stimulus with relatively lower weight. This approach will allow you to train muscles more effectively since you'll have less systemic fatigue from traditional powerlifting movements and approach to main movements.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:42:11.418Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Legs","Pull","Day 3","Rest","Legs","Pull","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":6.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Goblet Squat","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":6.5}]},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":6.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Med Ball Crunch","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":5,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":6.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":6.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","set